{
  "id": "pronouns-questions",
  "level": "A1",
  "title": "Wiederholung: Pronomen und Fragen",
  "group": "Basics",
  "sourceFile": "pronomfragen.html",
  "overview": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": "Question structure depends on whether the question has a question word. The conjugated verb comes immediately after a W-word; yes/no questions begin with the verb."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "content": "Subject pronouns and verb agreement"
      },
      {
        "type": "table",
        "content": "",
        "rows": [
          [
            "Pronoun",
            "kommen"
          ],
          [
            "ich",
            "komme"
          ],
          [
            "du",
            "kommst"
          ],
          [
            "er/sie/es",
            "kommt"
          ],
          [
            "wir",
            "kommen"
          ],
          [
            "ihr",
            "kommt"
          ],
          [
            "sie/Sie",
            "kommen"
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "table",
        "content": "",
        "rows": [
          [
            "Type",
            "Pattern",
            "Example"
          ],
          [
            "W-question",
            "W-word + verb + subject",
            "Wo wohnst du?"
          ],
          [
            "Yes/no",
            "Verb + subject + …",
            "Wohnst du in Berlin?"
          ],
          [
            "Statement",
            "Subject/topic + verb + …",
            "Du wohnst in Berlin."
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "content": "wer — who (subject)\nwen — whom (accusative)\nwem — whom (dative)\nwas — what\nwo / wohin / woher — where / to where / from where\nwann / warum / wie — when / why / how"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": "The question word already represents the missing information, so do not add another pronoun: Wer kommt? not Wer kommt er?"
      }
    ]
  },
